From: velzie <kveonl98@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Skip the Caps Lock entry of an SGCAPS pair in VkKeyScanEx.

In a keyboard layout's VK_TO_WCHARS table an entry with the SGCAPS
attribute holds the characters produced while Caps Lock is on, and the
entry following it holds the normal mapping; kbd_tables_vkey_to_wchar
already reads the pair that way. kbd_tables_wchar_to_vkey did not, and
matched the Caps Lock entry first. winewayland builds every letter of an
xkb layout as such a pair (Lock maps letters to their second level), so
VkKeyScanW('A') returned 0x41 and VkKeyScanW('a') 0x141 instead of 0x141
and 0x41. Skip SGCAPS entries when mapping a character back to a key.

---
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -503,6 +503,10 @@
     {
         for (entry = table->pVkToWchars; entry->VirtualKey; entry = NEXT_ENTRY(table, entry))
         {
+            /* An SGCAPS entry holds the mapping with Caps Lock on; the entry
+             * following it holds the mapping without, which is what
+             * VkKeyScan reports. */
+            if (entry->Attributes & SGCAPS) continue;
             for (mod = 0; mod < table->nModifications; ++mod)
             {
                 if (entry->wch[mod] == WCH_NONE || entry->wch[mod] != wch) continue;
